Project Description
The project involves the modernization or potential rebuild of the Connexus platform, a CRM-like tool used by Pfizer’s commercial oncology team—particularly Key Account Directors—to manage complex and dynamic relationships across territories. The platform supports coordination, insight sharing, and strategic planning across cross-functional teams.

👥 Key Stakeholder
David Jansen – Represents the commercial oncology team and is a key voice in defining the project’s direction and urgency.

Alex Boyce – Works closely with Zach and supports David; appears to be leading the technical and coordination aspects of the current platform.

Kelly Beeman – Identified as a senior decision-maker responsible for budget and executive sponsorship.

🎯 Project Goal
To transition Connexus to a more modern, maintainable, and user-friendly platform—potentially replacing Infosys as the current vendor—while preserving core functionality and improving usability. The ideal timeline for full transition is by Q2 or Q3 of next year, with a focus on doing it right rather than rushing.

